\c 1
\v 1 Blessed is the man who has not walked in the counsel of the ungodly, nor stood in the way of sinners, nor sat in the seat of scoffers.
\v 2 But his delight is in the law of the Lord, and on his law he will meditate day and night.
\v 3 He will be like a tree planted beside flowing waters that yields its fruit in due season; its leaf never withers, and all that he does will prosper.
\v 4 Not so the ungodly, not so, for they are like the chaff that the wind drives away from the face of earth.
\v 5 Therefore the ungodly shall not rise in judgement, nor sinners in the council of the righteous.
\v 6 For the Lord knows the way of the righteous, but the way of the ungodly will perish.
\c 2
\v 1 Why did the nations rage and the peoples contemplate vain things?
\v 2 The kings of the earth stood up, and the rulers gathered themselves together against the Lord and against his anointed, saying,
\v 3 ‘Let us tear their bonds asunder, and let us cast off their yoke from us.’
\v 4 He who dwells in the heavens will laugh at them; and the Lord will hold them in derision.
\v 5 Then he will speak to them in his anger, and trouble them in his rage.
\v 6 ‘But I was appointed king by him upon Sion, his holy mountain,
\v 7 proclaiming his commandment.
\p The Lord said to me, “You are my son, this day I have begotten you.
\v 8 Ask of me, and I shall give you the nations for your inheritance, and the ends of the earth for your possession.
\v 9 You will shepherd them with a rod of iron; you will break them like a potter's vessel.”’
\v 10 Now understand, you kings; be instructed, all you who judge the earth.
\v 11 Serve the Lord with fear, and rejoice in him with trembling.
\v 12 Seize instruction, or else the Lord may be angry, and you would perish from the righteous way when his rage is suddenly kindled.
\p Blessed are all those who trust in him.
\c 3
\v 1 Why, O Lord, are they multiplied who afflict me? Many rise up against me.
\v 2 Many say to my soul, ‘There is no salvation for him in his God.’
\mt3 ~~~
\v 3 But you, O Lord, are my protector, my glory, and the one who lifts up my head.
\v 4 I cried out to the Lord with my voice, and he heard me from his holy mountain.
\mt3 ~~~
\v 5 I lay down and slept; I awoke, for the Lord will help me.
\v 6 I will not be afraid of tens of thousands of people who set themselves against me on every side.
\v 7 Arise, O Lord; save me, my God, for you struck all who, without cause, are my adversaries; you broke the teeth of sinners.
\v 8 Salvation is of the Lord, and your blessing is upon your people.  
\c 4
\v 1 When I called upon him, the God of my righteousness heard me. In affliction, you enlarged me. Have mercy on me, and hear my prayer.
\v 2 You sons of men, how long will you be slow of heart? Why do you love vanity and look for what is false?
\mt3 ~~~
\v 3 But know also that the Lord made wondrous his holy one; the Lord shall hear me when I cry out to him.
\v 4 Be angry, but do not sin; feel compunction upon your beds for what you say in your hearts.
\mt3 ~~~
\v 5 Offer a sacrifice of righteousness, and hope in the Lord.
\v 6 Many say, ‘Who will show us good things?’ The light of your countenance, O Lord, was made manifest upon us.
\v 7 You gave great joy to my heart. In due season they were filled with their corn and wine and oil.
\v 8 In peace, I will lie down and sleep, for you alone, O Lord, settled me in hope.
\c 5
\v 1 Listen to my words, O Lord; attend to my cry.
\v 2 Hear the voice of my supplication, my king and my God, for to you, O Lord, I shall pray.
\v 3 In the morning, you will hear my voice; in the morning, I shall stand before you and you will look upon me.
\v 4 For you are not a God who desires lawlessness, neither shall the evildoer dwell with you.
\v 5 Lawbreakers shall not remain before your eyes. You hate all those who practise lawlessness.
\v 6 You will destroy all those who speak lies. A man of blood and deceit, the Lord abhors.
\v 7 But I, through the abundance of your mercy, will enter into your house; I shall worship towards your holy temple in fear of you.
\v 8 Lead me, O Lord, in your righteousness, because of my enemies; make straight my way before you.
\v 9 For there is no truth in their mouth, their heart is vain; their throat is an open tomb; with their tongues they deceive.
\v 10 Judge them, O God, let them fall by their own schemes; cast them out because of their many ungodly deeds, for they rebelled against you, O Lord.
\v 11 But let all who hope in you be glad. They shall rejoice for ever, and you will dwell among them; and all those who love your name shall glory in you.
\v 12 For you will bless the righteous, O Lord; you have adorned us with your good favour as with a shield.  
\c 6
\v 1 Do not rebuke me in your anger, O Lord, nor chasten me in your wrath.
\v 2 Have mercy on me, O Lord, for I am weak. Heal me, O Lord, for my bones are troubled.
\v 3 My soul is grievously troubled; but you, O Lord, how long?
\v 4 Return, O Lord; rescue my soul; save me because of your mercy.
\v 5 For in death there is no remembrance of you, and who will profess you in Hades?
\v 6 I am wearied with my groaning; every night I bathe my bed, I water my couch with tears.
\v 7 My eye is troubled with anger, I grow old among all my enemies.
\v 8 Depart from me, all you workers of lawlessness, for the Lord heard the voice of my weeping.
\v 9 The Lord heard my supplication; the Lord favourably received my prayer.
\v 10 Let all my enemies be ashamed and disquieted; let them be turned back and very quickly disgraced.
\c 7
\v 1 O Lord my God, I hope in you; save me from all those who persecute me, and rescue me.
\v 2 Or else, like a lion, at any time they may seize my soul, with no one to redeem or to save.
\v 3 O Lord my God, if I have done this, if there is unrighteousness on my hands,
\v 4 if I rendered evil to those who rendered evil to me, then let me fall empty before my enemies.
\v 5 Let the enemy pursue and overtake my soul and trample my life to the ground, and grind my glory into the dust.
\mt3 ~~~
\v 6 Rise up, O Lord, in your anger. Be exalted on the borders of my enemies. Awake, O Lord my God, in the decree which you commanded.
\v 7 An assembly of peoples shall surround you; over it you will take your seat on high.
\v 8 The Lord will judge the peoples. Judge me, O Lord, according to my righteousness, and according to the innocence that is in me.
\v 9 The wickedness of sinners shall be brought to an end; and you will direct the righteous, O God, you who searches hearts and minds.
\v 10 Righteous is my help from the God, the Saviour of the upright in heart.
\v 11 God is a righteous judge, strong and patient, not aroused to anger every day.
\v 12 If you will not repent, he will brandish his sword. His bow is bent and made ready.
\v 13 On it he fitted the instruments of death; he prepared his arrows for those who burn.
\v 14 Behold he who was in labour with unrighteousness conceived sorrow, and he brought forth lawlessness.
\v 15 He dug a pit and sunk it deep, but he will fall into the hole that he made.
\v 16 His mischief will return upon his own head, and upon his own crown his unrighteousness shall descend.
\v 17 I will confess the Lord for his righteousness, and sing to the name of the Lord Most High.
\c 8
\v 1 O Lord, our Lord, how wonderful is your name through all the earth. For your majesty is exalted high above the heavens.
\v 2 Out of the mouths of children and of babes you fashioned praise because of your enemies, to destroy the foe and the avenger.
\v 3 For I shall behold the heavens, the works of your fingers, the moon and the stars which you established.
\v 4 What is man that you are mindful of him, or the son of man that you visit him?
\v 5 You made him a little less than the angels, and crowned him with glory and honour;
\v 6 and you set him over the works of your hands. You placed everything under his feet,
\v 7 all sheep and cattle, and all the beasts of the field;
\v 8 the birds of the air, the fish of the sea, and everything that makes its way through the paths of the sea.
\v 9 O Lord, our Lord, how wonderful is your name in all the earth.  
\c 9
\v 1 I shall confess you, O Lord, with my whole heart, I shall recount all your wonders.
\v 2 I shall be glad, and rejoice in you. I shall sing to your name, O Most High.
\v 3 When my enemies are turned back, they will be weakened, and they will perish before your face.
\v 4 For you maintained my right and my cause; you sat enthroned, judging with righteousness.
\v 5 You rebuked the nations, and the ungodly perished; you blotted out their name from age to age and for ever.
\v 6 The enemy’s swords have failed for ever, and their cities you destroyed. Their memorial has been destroyed with a great roar.
\v 7 But the Lord abides for ever; he prepares his throne for judgement.
\v 8 He will judge the world in equity; he will judge the peoples with justice.
\v 9 The Lord became a refuge for the poor, a helper in times of affliction.
\v 10 Let those who know your name hope in you, O Lord, for you do not forsake those who seek you.
\v 11 Sing to the Lord who dwells in Sion; declare his ways among the nations.
\v 12 For while avenging blood, he remembered them; he did not forget the cry of the poor.
\v 13 Have mercy on me, O Lord; look upon my humiliation by my enemies, you who raises me up from the gates of death,
\v 14 that I may declare all your praises in the gates of the daughter of Sion. I will rejoice in your salvation.
\v 15 The nations are caught in the destruction that they prepared. Their foot is caught in the very snare that they hid.
\v 16 The Lord is known when he executes judgements; the sinner is caught in the works of his own hands.
\mt3 ~~~
\v 17 Let the sinners be turned away to Hades, all the nations that forget God.
\v 18 For the poor will never be forgotten; the endurance of the poor will never perish.
\v 19 Arise, O Lord, let not man prevail; let the nations be judged before you.
\v 20 Appoint a lawgiver over them, O Lord; let the nations know that they are but men.
\mt3 ~~~
\v 21 Why do you stand far off, O Lord? Why do you neglect us in times of affliction?
\v 22 While the ungodly act with pride, the poor are set on fire; they are caught in the schemes which they devised.
\v 23 For the sinner applauds the cravings of his soul, and the one who acts unrighteously blesses himself.
\v 24 The sinner provokes the Lord; because of the abundance of his anger he does not seek him; God is not before his eyes.
\v 25 His ways are profane at all times. Your laws are removed from before his sight. He will dominate all his enemies.
\v 26 For he said in his heart, ‘I shall not be shaken. From generation to generation, I shall be without adversity.’
\v 27 His mouth is filled with cursing, bitterness and deceit; under his tongue are weariness and misery.
\v 28 With the rich in secret places he lies in ambush to kill the innocent; his eyes are set on the poor.
\v 29 He lies in wait in secret, like a lion in its den. He lies in ambush to catch the poor, to snatch the poor one and drag him away.
\v 30 In his snare he shall humble him.
\p But he will stoop down and fall when he dominates the needy.
\v 31 For he says in his heart, ‘God has forgotten; he has turned his face away, he never sees.’
\v 32 Rise up, O Lord my God, and let your hand be lifted up, and never forget your poor.
\v 33 Why do the ungodly provoke God? For he says in his heart, ‘God will not require an account.’
\v 34 But you do see, you who perceive misery and rage, that you may take them into your hands. The poor are left to you; you are a helper to the orphan.
\v 35 Break the arm of the sinner and the evil-doer. His sin shall be sought out, and he will not be found.
\v 36 The Lord reigns from age to age and for ever; but you nations shall perish from his land.
\v 37 O Lord, you have heard the desire of the poor; your ear inclined to their readiness of heart,
\v 38 to judge for the fatherless and the humble so that man may no longer boast upon the earth.
\c 10
\v 1 In the Lord I trust. How then shall you say to my soul, ‘Flee like a sparrow to the mountains?’
\v 2 For you see the sinners stretch tight their bow; they prepare their arrows for the quiver, to shoot at the upright in heart when the moon gives no light.
\v 3 For they destroy the things that you made; but what has the righteous man done?
\v 4 The Lord is in his holy temple; the Lord’s throne is in heaven. His eyes behold the poor; and his gaze examines the sons of men.
\v 5 The Lord examines the righteous and the ungodly; but he who loves unrighteousness hates his own soul.
\v 6 He shall rain down snares upon sinners; fire and brimstone and stormy winds shall be the portion of their cup.
\v 7 For the Lord is righteous and loves righteousness; his face beholds what is upright.
\c 11
\v Save me, O Lord, for there is now no one holy. The truthful have declined among the sons of men.
\v Each speaks vanity to his neighbour; with deceitful lips, and with a double heart they speak.
\v May the Lord destroy all deceitful lips, and the boastful tongue of those who say,
\v ‘We will extol our tongues, our lips are our own; who is Lord over us?’
\v Because of the suffering of the poor and the groaning of the needy, ‘I will now arise,’ says the Lord. ‘I will set them in safety, and I will speak openly with them.’
\v The words of the Lord are pure words, like silver purified, seven times refined, in the earthen furnace.
\v You, O Lord, shall guard us, and preserve us from this generation, and for ever.
\v The ungodly walk around in circles. According to the heights of your greatness, you take great care of the sons of men.

PSALM 12
\v How long, O Lord, shall you forget me? For ever? How long shall you turn your face from me?
\v How long shall I take counsel in my soul, having sorrow in my heart day and night? How long shall my enemy be exalted over me?
\v Look on me, and hear me, O Lord my God. Give light to my eyes, lest at any time I should sleep in death;
\v lest at any time my enemy may say, ‘I prevailed against him.’ Those who trouble me shall rejoice greatly should I be shaken.
\v But I hope in your mercy; my heart rejoices in your salvation. I will sing to the Lord who deals bountifully with me, and I will sing to the name of the Lord Most High.

PSALM 13
\v The fool says in his heart, ‘There is no God.’
\v They are corrupt, and have become abhorrent in their ways. There is not one doing good.
\v The Lord looked down from heaven on the sons of men, to see if there were any who understood, or who sought after God.
\v They have all turned away; they have altogether become useless. There is not one doing good, not even one.
\v Do they not know, all those who work lawlessness, those who devour my people as though they were eating bread?
\v They did not call upon the Lord; they were timid with fear, where there was no fear. But God is with the generation of the righteous.
\v You dishonoured the counsel of the poor, but the Lord is his hope.
\v Who shall bring the salvation of Israel from Sion?
\v When the Lord returns his people from captivity, Jacob shall rejoice and Israel shall be glad.

Glory to the Father, and to the Son, and to the Holy Spirit, now and ever, and to ages of ages. Amen.
Alleluia, alleluia, alleluia. Glory to you, O God (x 3).
Lord, have mercy (x 3).
Glory to the Father, etc.

Stasis 3
PSALM 14
\v O Lord, who shall dwell in your tabernacle? Who may pitch their tent on your holy mountain?
\v He who walks without blame, and practises righteousness, and who speaks truth in his heart,
\v who utters no deceit with his tongue, nor does evil to his neighbour, nor takes up a reproach against those who dwell near him.
\v In his sight evildoers are reckoned as nothing, but he glorifies those who fear the Lord. 
\v He who gives an oath to his neighbour and does not break it; he who does not lend his money at interest, and takes no bribes against the innocent.
\v He who does these things shall never be shaken.

PSALM 15
\v Preserve me, O Lord, for I hope in you.
\v I said to the Lord, ‘You are my God, and you have no need of my goods.’
\v In the holy ones who are in his land, in them the Lord made wonderful all his will.
\v Their infirmities were multiplied, and after this they made haste. I will not join their assemblies of blood offerings, nor will I make mention of their names with my lips.
\v The Lord is the portion of my inheritance and of my cup; it is you who restores my inheritance to me.
\v The measuring lines fell to me in the most excellent places, and my inheritance is most splendid to me.
\v I will bless the Lord who gives me understanding; even to until it is night, my heart corrects me.
\v I set the Lord always in my sight, for he is at my right hand so that I may not be shaken.
\v Therefore my heart was glad, and my tongue rejoiced; my flesh also shall live in hope.
\v For you shall not abandon my soul in Hades, nor shall you allow your holy one to see corruption.
\v You make known to me the ways of life. Your presence shall fill me with joy; at your right hand are delights without end.

PSALM 16
\v Pay heed, O Lord, to my righteousness; attend to my supplication. Hear my prayer, which does not proceed from deceitful lips.
\v Let my judgement come from your presence; let my eyes behold righteousness.
\v You tested my heart, you visited me in the night; you tried me as with fire, and unrighteousness was not found in me.
\v That my mouth may not speak of the works of men, through the words of your lips I kept to hard ways.
\v Hold fast my steps on your paths, that my footsteps may not falter.
\v I cried out, O God, and you heard me. Incline your ear to me, and listen to my words.
\v Make wonderful your mercies, you who saves those who hope in you.
\v From those who resist your right hand, guard me as the apple of your eye. Protect me under the shelter of your wings from the face of the ungodly who afflict me.
\v My enemies surrounded my soul. They enclose themselves in their own fat; their mouth speaks arrogance.
\v Having cast me out, they now surround me; they set their eyes turned down to the earth.
\v They lie wait for me like a lion eager for prey, and like a young lion that lurks in hiding.
\v Rise up, O Lord, overtake them and cause them to stumble. By your sword, rescue my soul from the ungodly, from the enemies of your hand.
\v O Lord, destroy them from the earth, scatter them because of their life. With your hidden stores their belly is filled. They satisfy themselves with swine, and leave what remains to their little ones.
\v But I will appear in righteousness before your face; I will be satisfied when your glory is revealed.

Glory to the Father, and to the Son, and to the Holy Spirit, now and ever, and to ages of ages. Amen.
Alleluia, alleluia, alleluia. Glory to you, O God (x 3).
Lord, have mercy (x 3).
Glory to the Father, etc.

SUNDAY MATINS B

KATHISMA 3
Stasis 1
PSALM 17
\v I will love you, O Lord, my strength.
\v The Lord is my firm foundation and my refuge and my deliverer. My God is my helper and I will hope in him, my protector, the horn of my salvation and my support.
\v With praise I will call upon the Lord, and I will be saved from my enemies.
\v The sorrows of death surrounded me, and the torrents of lawlessness greatly troubled me.
\v The anguish of Hades engulfed me, and the snares of death overtook me.
\v In my affliction, I called upon the Lord, and I cried out to my God. From his holy temple, he heard my voice, and my cry before him reached his ears.
\v Then the earth shook and trembled. The foundations of the mountains were troubled, and they shook because God was angry with them.
\v Smoke went up in his wrath, and fire blazed from his presence; coals were kindled by it.
\v He bowed the heavens and came down, and darkness was under his feet.
\v He ascended upon the cherubim and flew, he flew upon the wings of the winds.
\v He made darkness his cover, his tabernacle round about him, dark waters in the clouds of the air.
\v From the brightness before him, clouds, hailstones, and coals of fire were dispersed.
\v The Lord thundered from heaven, and the Most High spoke out with his voice.
\v He sent out arrows and scattered them; he multiplied lightning and troubled them.
\v The fountainheads of the waters appeared, and the foundations of the world were laid bare at your rebuke, O Lord, at the blast of the breath of your wrath.
\v He sent from on high, and took me; he drew me to himself out of many waters.
\v He shall rescue me from my powerful enemies, and from those who hate me, for they are stronger than I am.
\v They overtook me in the day of my affliction, and the Lord became my protector.
\v He brought me out into an open space. He shall deliver me, because he delights in me.
\v The Lord shall reward me according to my righteousness, and he shall repay me according to the cleanness of my hands.
\v For I kept the ways of the Lord, and did not turn to ungodliness, away from my God.
\v For all his judgements are before me, and his statutes I did not thrust from me.
\v I will be blameless with him, and shall guard myself from my lawlessness.
\v The Lord shall reward me according to my righteousness, and according to the cleanness of my hands before his eyes.
\v With the holy, you shall be holy, and with the innocent, you shall be innocent, and with the chosen, you shall be chosen.
\v But with the crooked, you shall be perverse, for you shall save a lowly people, but bring low the eyes of the proud.
\v For you, O Lord, shall light my lamp; you, O my God, shall enlighten my darkness.
\v For by you, will I be rescued from marauding hordes, and by my God, I will pass over the wall.
\v My God: his way is undefiled; the words of the Lord are tried by fire. He is the protector of all those who hope in him.
\v For who is God, but the Lord? And who is God, except for our God?
\v It is God, who girded me with strength and made my way blameless;
\v he, who made ready my feet, like the feet of the stag, and set me upon high places; he, who trains my hands for war.
\v You made my arms like a bow of bronze; you gave me the shield of your saving help, and your right hand upheld me.
\v Your discipline completely restored me; and this, your discipline, shall teach me.
\v You widened my stride beneath me, and my footsteps are not feeble.
\v I will pursue my enemies and overtake them, and I will not turn back until they are no more.
\v I will break them, and they shall not be able to stand. They shall fall beneath my feet.
\v For you girded me with strength for battle; you subdued under me those who rose up against me.
\v You made my enemies turn their backs to me, and destroyed those who hated me.
\v They cried out, but there was no one to save them; even to the Lord, but he did not listen to them.
\v I will grind them fine as dust before the wind, and I will trample them down like mire in the streets.
\v You shall deliver me from disputes with people; you shall appoint me as the ruler of nations.
\v A people whom I did not know served me; when their ears heard, they obeyed me.
\v The sons of strangers lied to me; these sons of strangers grew old and limped from their paths.
\v The Lord lives. Blessed is my God, and let the God of my salvation be exalted, the God who avenges me and subdues the peoples under me.
\v My rescuer from my enraged enemies, you shall lift me up above those who rise up against me. From the unrighteous man you shall rescue me.
\v Therefore, O Lord, I will profess you among the nations, and to your name will I sing.
\v I will magnify him who gives deliverance to his king, and shows mercy to David, his anointed, and to his seed for ever.

Glory to the Father, and to the Son, and to the Holy Spirit, now and ever, and to ages of ages. Amen.
Alleluia, alleluia, alleluia. Glory to you, O God (x 3)
Lord, have mercy (x 3).
Glory to the Father, etc.

Stasis 2
PSALM 18
\v The heavens declare the glory of God, and the firmament proclaims the work of his hands.
\v Day speaks to day, and night to night declares knowledge.
\v There is no speech nor language in which their voices are not heard.
\v Their sound goes out into all the earth, and their words to the ends of the world.
\v He set his tabernacle in the sun; and he, like a bridegroom coming out from his bride’s chamber, rejoices like a strong man to run his course.
\v From one end of the heavens he sets out with the furthest end of the heavens as his goal, and there is no one who can hide from his heat.
\v The law of the Lord is perfect, converting souls; the testimony of the Lord is trustworthy, giving wisdom to infants.
\v The ordinances of the Lord are upright, making the heart rejoice; the commandment of the Lord is radiant, lighting up the eyes.
\v The fear of the Lord is holy, enduring from age to age; the laws of the Lord are true, and all of them just.
\v They are more to be desired than gold and many precious stones, and they are sweeter than honey and the honeycomb.
\v Indeed, your servant keeps them; and in keeping them there is great reward.
\v Transgressions? Who shall comprehend them? From my hidden sins, cleanse me.
\v From those of others, spare your servant. If they have no dominion over me, then I will be blameless and cleansed of great sin.
\v Let the words of my mouth and the meditation of my heart  be always pleasing in your sight, O Lord, my helper and my redeemer.

PSALM 19
\v May the Lord hear you in the day of tribulation; may the name of the God of Jacob protect you.
\v May he send you help from the holy place, and may he support you from Sion.
\v May he remember every one of your sacrifices, and cherish your whole-burnt offering.
\v \mt3 ~~~
\v May he give to you according to your heart, and fulfil all of your plans.
\v We will rejoice in your salvation, and in the name of our God will we glory.
\v May the Lord fulfil all of your petitions.
\v Now I know that the Lord saved his anointed. He shall hear him from his holy heaven; the saving help of his right hand is mighty.
\v Some glory in chariots and some in horses, but we, in the name of the Lord our God.
\v They were shackled and fell, but we arose and are set upright.
\v O Lord, save the king, and hear us on the day when we call upon you.

PSALM 20
\v O Lord, in your strength the king shall be glad, and he shall rejoice greatly in your salvation.
\v You granted him the desire of his heart, and did not withhold from him the request of his lips.
\v \mt3 ~~~
\v For you went before him with the blessings of kindness. You set upon his head a crown of precious stones.
\v He asked you for life, and you gave him length of days from age to age.
\v Great is his glory through your salvation; glory and majesty shall you bestow upon him.
\v From age to age you shall give him blessings; you shall make him glad with the joy of your presence.
\v For the king hopes in the Lord, and through the mercy of the Most High, he shall not be shaken.
\v Let your hand be found for all your enemies; may your right hand find all who hate you.
\v For you shall make them like a fiery furnace at the time of your presence. The Lord shall throw them into confusion in his anger, and fire shall devour them.
\v You shall destroy their offspring from the earth, and their descendants from among the sons of men.
\v For they intended evils against you; they devised a plan which they are powerless to enact.
\v For you shall cause them to turn their back; in your remnant, you shall prepare their face.
\v Be exalted, O Lord, in your power. We will sing and praise your mighty acts.

Glory to the Father, and to the Son, and to the Holy Spirit, now and ever, and to ages of ages. Amen.
Alleluia, alleluia, alleluia. Glory to you, O God (x 3).
Lord, have mercy (x 3).
Glory to the Father, etc.

Stasis 3
PSALM 21
\v O God, my God, attend to me; why have you forsaken me? Far from my salvation are the words of my transgressions.
\v My God, I will cry out by day, but you shall not hear; and by night, and it shall not be folly for me.
\v But you dwell in the holy place, the praise of Israel.
\v Our fathers hoped in you, they hoped and you delivered them.
\v They cried out to you, and they were saved; in you they hoped, and they were not put to shame.
\v But I am a worm, and not a man, a reproach of men, and despised by people.
\v All those who looked upon me mocked me; they spoke with their lips and shook their head,
\v ‘He hoped in the Lord; let him rescue him, let him save him since he delights in him.’
\v For it was you who drew me from the womb, my hope from my mother’s breasts.
\v I was cast upon you from the womb. From my mother's womb you have been my God.
\v Do not stand far from me, for affliction is near; there is no one to help me.
\v Many young bulls surrounded me; fat bulls encircled me.
\v They opened their mouths against me, like the lion that rages and roars.
\v I was poured out like water, and disjointed were all my bones. My heart was like melting wax within my breast.
\v My strength was dried up like charred clay, and my tongue clung to my throat; you brought me down to the dust of death.
\v For many dogs encircled me, an assembly of evildoers surrounded me. They pierced my hands and my feet.
\v They counted all my bones; they gazed at me and stared.
\v They divided my garments among themselves, and for my clothing they cast lots.
\v But you, O Lord, do not remove your help far away from me; attend to my support.
\v Rescue my soul from the sword, and my only-begotten from the paw of the dog.
\v Save me from the mouth of the lion; and my lowliness from the horns of one-horned beasts.
\v I will declare your name to my brethren; in the midst of the assembly I will sing a hymn to you.
\v You, who fear the Lord, praise him; all you offspring of Jacob, glorify him; let all the offspring of Israel fear him.
\v For he did not despise or scorn the supplication of the poor, nor did he turn his face from me; and when I cried out to him, he heard me.
\v My praise is from you in the great assembly. In the sight of those who fear you, I will fulfil my vows.
\v The poor shall eat and be satisfied, and those who seek the Lord shall praise him; their hearts shall live from age to age.
\v All the ends of the earth shall remember and turn to the Lord, and all the families of the nations shall worship before him.
\v For the kingdom is the Lord's, and he has dominion over the nations.
\v All the prosperous on the earth ate and worshipped; all those who go down into the earth shall fall down before him.
\v My soul lives for him, and my offspring shall serve him. The coming generation shall be told of the Lord.
\v They shall proclaim his righteousness to a people yet to be born, that the Lord made them.

PSALM 22
\v The Lord shepherds me, and there is nothing I shall want.
\v In a place of green pasture he made me dwell; by restful waters he nurtured me.
\v He restored my soul. He led me into paths of righteousness for his name’s sake.
\v Even though I should walk in the midst of the shadow of death I will fear no evil. For you are with me; your rod and your staff, they comfort me.
\v You prepared a table before me, in the presence of those who afflict me. You anointed my head with oil; and your cup that inebriates me is the best.
\v Your mercy shall follow me all the days of my life; and I will dwell in the house of the Lord for length of days.
\v 
PSALM 23
\v The earth is the Lord’s and all its fullness, the world and all who dwell in it. For he founded it on the seas and prepared it on the rivers.
\v Who shall ascend the mountain of the Lord, or who shall stand in his holy place?
\v He whose hands are clean and whose heart is pure; he who does not occupy his soul with what is vain, or swear deceitfully to his neighbour.
\v He shall receive a blessing from the Lord, and mercy from God his Saviour.
\v This is the generation of those who seek the Lord, who seek the face of the God of Jacob.
\mt3 ~~~
\v Lift up the gates, you rulers, and be lifted up, you everlasting gates, and the king of Glory shall enter.
\v Who is this king of Glory? The Lord, strong and mighty, the Lord mighty in battle.
\v Lift up the gates, you rulers; and be lifted up, you everlasting gates; and the king of Glory shall enter.
\v Who is this king of Glory? The Lord of hosts, he is the king of Glory!

